 },
 "notes": "Mohod et al. (Cureus 2026) report a hospital-wide antibiogram of 4,603 culture-positive isolates from all specimens at Indira Gandhi Government Medical College, Nagpur, May 2024 to April 2025. It covers E. coli (1,321), K. pneumoniae (1,051), P. aeruginosa (785), Acinetobacter (479, shown as A. baumannii), S. aureus (664), E. faecalis (98), E. faecium (54) and Salmonella Typhi (11). The tables print % resistant, so figures are 100 minus %R and intermediate counts as susceptible. Colistin, tested by MIC, showed no resistance in any Gram-negative organism. Nitrofurantoin and fosfomycin were tested on urinary isolates only, and the enterococcal gentamicin figure is high-level gentamicin. MRSA was 48.72%, inducible clindamycin resistance 21.97% and VRE 0.77%. Salmonella Typhi figures come from the paper's text, not a table, and rest on 11 isolates.",
